<title>JAPAN: Oji steady at midday after merger.</title>
<headline>Oji steady at midday after merger.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Oji Paper Co Ltd, which was created on Tuesday through a merger of two major Japanese paper producers, were unchanged after its first half-day session.</p>
<p>Oji Paper's share price stood at 845 yen at midday on Tuesday, unchanged from the share price of its predecessor New Oji Paper Co Ltd at the close on Monday.</p>
<p>New Oji Paper and Honshu Paper Co Ltd merged on Tuesday to become the third-largest paper and pulp producer in the world. Honshu was dissolved on the merger.</p>
</text>
